    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="0468" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.76/6–446: Telegrams</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pawley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-28T20:00:00-04:00">June 28, 1946—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>885. Emb. desp. 5216 June 4. It was Depts understanding Navy had requested you
                    obtain extension right to operate Recife radio direction finder station. If no
                    action yet taken pls approach Braz Govt in effort obtain consent, preferably in
                    writing, to continued use this station for indefinite period or for as long a
                    time as possible.</p>
                <p>Chief Naval Operations has authorized Naval Attaché Rio abandon fixed
                    installations Belém and Bahia stations and you may support your request by
                    presenting these installations to Braz Govt (Emb Airgram A–512 May 22<anchor
                        n="47" xml:id="d400-f1"/>). Naval Attaché has also been authorized declare
                    equipment at Belém and Bahia stations to FLC as surplus. (Deptel 847 June
                        24<anchor n="47" xml:id="d400-f2"/>). Only if necessary to clinch right to
                    continue operation at Recife you are authorized arrange with FLC Bio for
                    negotiation transfer this equipment to Braz Govt without cost but in this case
                    Navy must arrange reimbursement to FLC of appraised value equipment
                    transferred.</p>
                <p>Consult with Gen. Miller<anchor n="48" xml:id="d400-f3"/> as to desirability
                    making this approach prior conclusion of bulk sale.</p>
                <p>Keep Dept currently informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
